{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert","id":903871,"title":"Dark Eras 2e Changeling Review *Spoiler Alert*","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-30T17:40:58-07:00","id":903871,"title":"Dark Eras 2e Changeling Review *Spoiler Alert*","content":"SPOILER ALERT.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so I'll get the straight forward ones out of the way. Loved Three Kingdoms Changelings, the new 2e directional courts are awesome, with their capstone mantle ability of each court is interesting and useful.<br /> <br /> The directional contracts are useful and flavourful, but Changing Winds would likely have to be regulated by the local Freeholds, and I can see none directional court Freeholds making it illegal altogether, it could cause way to much chaos.<br /> <br /> I think the Mandate of Heaven is the Bulwark of the Directional Court, even if it doesn't say so in so many words.<br /> <br /> I also loved the Victorian Changeling, great courts, cool contracts, in fact some of my favourite contracts. Adored every single contract and I'd happily used them all.<br /> <br /> Contract of Abjuration is freaking brutal, a great tool to fight other supernatural splats.<br /> <br /> Contracts of Air and Darkness could be so much fun, especially for Darklings. Really looking forward to using that one.<br /> <br /> Now for the Grimms.<br /> <br /> My favourite parts were the the Grimm Seeming and the magic beans! Love the magic beans.<br /> <br /> Now the Grimms, to fix the Grimms I'd just make the none clarity part of the Seeming Blessing, the exact opposite of the Seeming curse, as long as the Grimm stays in a role, attempts to evade the Gentry and Huntsmen recieve the rote quality.<br /> <br /> So Seeming Contract Affinity, I'd just have Grimm pick the Seeming that they feel closest to (aside from the Grimms of course) and use their Seeming Affinities for now. A temp solution for the Grimms.<br /> <br /> I do wish the mechinical effects of assuming a rolenwere clearer. I think your mien shifts to the role.<br /> <br /> The other trifles and tokens were wonderful.<br /> <br /> I liked the Entitlements, and I wonder if they accurately represent how entitlements are handled in 2e. So far they look alot like they did in 1e. Still cool entitlements.<br /> <br /> I really loved the Inspirational Media section.including philosphical material was inspired.<br /> <br /> Requiem of a Dream (may have messed the title up), isn't just a book its a movie with Jennifer Connelly, who I've been a fan of since I was a kid watching Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> The contracts don't have Seeming affinities, but as they only workon Childern, I doubt anyone who isn't focused on Childern as a plotline/theme for their Character in a major way, will every take them permantly. It makes make sense to use a Goblin Vow to gain temp access when needed, so the little issues aren't going to cause a major issue.<br /> <br /> I like the courts of the Arts and the Sciences, I can see this being a common court in University Towns, although I can see regional difference like adding a History, Theology, Philosphy, or Social Science Courts (the social science court who be a split in the science court, with the old science court becoming the hard science court).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T17:59:55-07:00","id":903877,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the Three Kingdoms was probably my second/third favorite in the book (First is Sundered World, the other is Beneath the Skin-I like weird fantasy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:15:59-07:00","id":904168,"title":"","content":"Some of the little blurbs on other supernaturals in the none changing eras can be really useful.<br /> <br /> The Demons Berlin Changeling blurb actually fits really well as a result of what happened during the brothers Grimm era of Germany and its Demon blurb.<br /> <br /> During the Grimm Era, the increased amount of Gentry in German, some how appears to have caused the influence of the God Macchine in Germany to be greatly diminished.<br /> <br /> Hundreds of years later the God Machine has great influence in Berlin, and the Summwr Court has largely tamed the local hedge creating a golden age for German Changelings, which means a diminished influence for the Gentry, to the point where the then Winter Court fears an alliance amoung the Gentry will result.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that the God Machine is secretly supporting the Changelings of the Summer Court in the hopes of undermining the Gentry in Berlin and likely throughout Germany.<br /> <br /> If the Gentry ever find out, it could lead to a war between not the Changelings and the Gentry, but outright war between the Gentry and the God Machine, perhaps in a later time period like the Present.<br /> <br /> I also wonder if Pangaeans travelled into the Hedge. I mean if some had access to the Fate Arcana, then there is no reason why they couldn't open a gateway to the Hedge and flee beyond the reach of Father Wolf.<br /> <br /> Perhaps some some unusually powerful Hobgoblins and Hedge Beasts were former Pangaeans who used the Hedge as a refuge from Father Wolf.<br /> <br /> Now for the Skinchanger Merit, what if a Skinchanger found out about the Gentry and learned how to make a skin out one of the Gentry by some miracle.<br /> <br /> It would be a mortal could become a member of the Gentry and would likely be treated as such by the Gentry, but an observant Changeling would know the different and could use said Skin Thief to their advantage. And one wonders what would happen if said Skin Thief visited Arcadia.<br /> <br /> You would have to change the Essence Pool Merit to Glamour Pool, and Spirit Power to Fae Power (getting Pledges, possibly including Goblin Vows instead of Influences and Contracts instead of numena or manifestations.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:36:54-07:00","id":904505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert#post903871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now for the Grimms.<br /> <br /> My favourite parts were the the Grimm Seeming and the magic beans! Love the magic beans.<br /> <br /> Now the Grimms, to fix the Grimms I'd just make the none clarity part of the Seeming Blessing, the exact opposite of the Seeming curse, as long as the Grimm stays in a role, attempts to evade the Gentry and Huntsmen recieve the rote quality.<br /> <br /> So Seeming Contract Affinity, I'd just have Grimm pick the Seeming that they feel closest to (aside from the Grimms of course) and use their Seeming Affinities for now. A temp solution for the Grimms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty good stopgap, actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert#post903871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wish the mechinical effects of assuming a rolenwere clearer. I think your mien shifts to the role.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. That's why I created the Storybook Life Merit. It really seems that with the focus on roles that the Grimm Seeming had, that they would have given a bit more info on those. If they are allowed to just choose and switch roles at will, then their Seeming curse would never really come into play.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:18:43-07:00","id":904536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert#post903871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked the Entitlements, and I wonder if they accurately represent how entitlements are handled in 2e. So far they look alot like they did in 1e. Still cool entitlements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only take credit for the imaginary friends Entitlement, but I'm so glad you liked it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert#post903871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really loved the Inspirational Media section.including philosphical material was inspired. <br /> <br /> Requiem of a Dream (may have messed the title up), isn't just a book its a movie with Jennifer Connelly, who I've been a fan of since I was a kid watching Labyrinth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extremely proud of this section, tbh. High praise. Thanks so much =).<br /> <br /> Make sure you watch <i>The 4400,</i> if you've never seen it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert#post903871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The contracts don't have Seeming affinities, but as they only work on children, I doubt anyone who isn't focused on children as a plotline/theme for their character in a major way, will ever take them permanently. It makes make sense to use a Goblin Vow to gain temp access when needed, so the little issues aren't going to cause a major issue.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I should probably have added in a line that the same mechanics could theoretically work for adults =/. I did intend to make something geared towards use with child characters, but you have my permission to take them for use with adults as well. Some 20-30% of adults still use comfort objects, including me *shrug*. If you'd like to use my Contracts for adults, go for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T17:09:41-07:00","id":904569,"title":"","content":"My smart phone is my comfort object, I call it the precious (Lord of the Rings reference).<br /> <br /> I'll add 4400 to the list of shows to watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T17:46:51-07:00","id":904597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert?p=904569#post904569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My smart phone is my comfort object, I call it the precious (Lord of the Rings reference).</div> </div> </div> </div>I still sleep with my comfort object from when I was five. True story. He's a stuffed Dalmatian and his name is Bubby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T04:49:56-07:00","id":904858,"title":"","content":"Random exortation, this post is what tipped the scales and made me bite the bullet and buy the book. I'm really glad I did, skimming the fluff, it looks amazing.<br /> <br /> As for mechanics. The Contracts are really great. Adjuration and Air/Shadow are the type of things I drool over. Contract of Blades is kind of good, but some of the powers feel over costed at first blush, or the whole set of contracts looks formatted to how 1e did things (1 to 5 scaling). The children contracts are interesting, but only targeting children is so very niche.<br /> <br /> The various Courts were very well written, and the examples help me better make my own courts. Really want to see Seasonal! But I understand why they weren't detailed.<br /> <br /> Skin stands out as a pleasant surprise, and I almost wonder if a Changeling could take it. It feels in theme for some changeling appropriate concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T05:14:23-07:00","id":904868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert?p=904858#post904858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the whole set of contracts looks formatted to how 1e did things (1 to 5 scaling). The children contracts are interesting, but only targeting children is so very niche.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said it in other places, but I know not everyone can see everything posted here--it's not how 1E did things, it's more like a 1.5E, and it's specifically how I was instructed to do it. Specifically how.<br /> <br /> And you have my personal permission to use my comfort objects contracts with adults if you would like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:23:20-07:00","id":905003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert?p=904868#post904868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've said it in other places, but I know not everyone can see everything posted here--it's not how 1E did things, it's more like a 1.5E, and it's specifically how I was instructed to do it. Specifically how.<br /> <br /> And you have my personal permission to use my comfort objects contracts with adults if you would like.</div> </div> </div> </div> The contracts are completely usable, you just can't take them at character creation.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling David was at an ealier stage of the Development process when he you your marching orders. Its why Dark Eras should have come AFTER Prommie 2e, Changeling 2e, Hunter 2e, Giest 2e, and Mummy 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:26:31-07:00","id":905006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert?p=905003#post905003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The contracts are completely usable, you just can't take them at character creation.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling David was at an ealier stage of the Development process when he you your marching orders. Its why Dark Eras should have come AFTER Prommie 2e, Changeling 2e, Hunter 2e, Giest 2e, and Mummy 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have taken so much longer, is the thing =/. And maybe that was best, doesn't matter, it's done now.<br /> <br /> So, with what we have, I'm really glad you like it. And I agree that it's usable. Maybe after Changeling 2E is out, I can post 2E versions here.<br /> <br /> But for now, I really appreciate that you like what I did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:13:05-07:00","id":905464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert?p=905006#post905006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would have taken so much longer, is the thing =/. And maybe that was best, doesn't matter, it's done now.<br /> <br /> So, with what we have, I'm really glad you like it. And I agree that it's usable. Maybe after Changeling 2E is out, I can post 2E versions here.<br /> <br /> But for now, I really appreciate that you like what I did.</div> </div> </div> </div> Excellent idea! Thank you I look forward to it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:14:05-07:00","id":905575,"title":"","content":"The Contracts of Air and Darkness have to be my favourite personally.<br /> <br /> Someone who has fully master it at 5 dots, can do incredible things, but even at one dot it can do really cool things.<br /> <br /> At 5 dots you can create the illusion that you just died, to get soneone off your back, that its cold in the middle of a burning inferno and those flames are will just darkness, create a castle that you can touch/taste/see/hear/smell with full movement of things like doors, create an orgy or battle where you can see/touch/taste/smell/hear the particpates, disguise yourself as an enemy and the enemy as yourself, when in darkness if your a Darkling you can create the illusion that their is visible light.<br /> <br /> The really funny thing is if you get all three Seeming Affinities, and create the illusion in darkness of a scary object in order to protect yourself, you get +9 dice and pay no glamour.<br /> <br /> Best starting Contract for a Darkling, especially from the start, but the question is can a Darkling not from the Ash Court take ot, like said a Darkling from the Ivory, Silver, Autum, Brass, North, Arts, or Unseelie Courts for example this is too awesome a Contract to keep it just tied to London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:40:57-07:00","id":905587,"title":"","content":"Even freaker, imagine people boating or swimming on a lake, and create the illusion that the air is water and the water is air,including switching the sensations of breathing and drowning. Great way to get a group of people to kill themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 06-02-2016, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:38:48-07:00","id":906009,"title":"","content":"Using Contracts of Inspiration, a Changeling could basically write down a book of spells that anyone could use to create a condition in the listeners. All the user would have to do is read the words to a &quot;spell&quot; out loud to trigger the effect with a manipulation + expression roll. I assume each would be single use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:56:15-07:00","id":906552,"title":"","content":"I wonder what all conditions you could give via that contract, that make sense. If it's really *any* condition then that is super broad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:51:22-07:00","id":907185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/903871-dark-eras-2e-changeling-review-spoiler-alert?p=906552#post906552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what all conditions you could give via that contract, that make sense. If it's really *any* condition then that is super broad.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, you could give the Acuity or Bewitched conditions, or Thrall, Soulless, Delusional, Spooked, Swoon, Wanton, ect... to those around you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T00:03:22-07:00","id":907492,"title":"","content":"You've got to get the ST to agree that a condition is appropriate for the words though. Spooked, sure, easily. Swooning- romantic poetry, awesome. Delusional... maaaaaybe with a super high target number and an excellent justification? But I think Soulless or Thrall is way beyond the scope of the Contract. Inspiration is essentially messing with people's head along the thematic lines of whatever words they're using and that's not going to remove their soul (not in my games anyways).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T06:20:30-07:00","id":907588,"title":"","content":"So thinking about what Conditions are potentially appropriate...<br /> <br /> Agoraphobic - &quot;People suck. You are a faceless nobody in a crowd that hates you.&quot;<br /> Atavism - Something that rouses ancestral, violent memories.<br /> Awestruck - A song, poetry, or speech just that beautiful.<br /> Berserk - Something that pisses everyone off.<br /> Bestial - Something that gets the crowd worked up and angry.<br /> Broken - A story that breaks the user's will, like a message to an enemy about how they're going to be destroyed. A threat.<br /> Charmed - A speech about how great and trustworthy someone is.<br /> Competitive - A pep talk before a game or a formally issued challenge.<br /> Confused - Nonsense.<br /> Connected - Teamwork building exorcises, or a speech to bring everyone together. Both the targets of the condition and the recipients must hear.<br /> Cowed - Some really witty comebacks or other tearing downs.<br /> Demoralized - &quot;You suck.&quot;<br /> Dependent - &quot;Guys, we *really* have to take care of this person.&quot;<br /> Delusional - Make someone believe you.<br /> Dominated - Hypnotic script, mundane-ish hypnosis.<br /> Easy Prey - &quot;So, this is totally definitely how you avoid being hunted.&quot; (And be wrong.)<br /> Ecstatic - Religious speech.<br /> Frightened - *Really* scary story about how terrible something is.<br /> Guilty - Something to make the audience feel guilty.<br /> Humbled - Read from the book of longinus.<br /> Informed - A lecture.<br /> Inspired - A motivational speech.<br /> Jaded - &quot;Humanity sucks.&quot;<br /> Leveraged - A sales pitch or speech convincing the audience they owe someone.<br /> Megalomaniacal - &quot;You are REALLY great. Here's why.&quot;<br /> Mesmerized - Hypnotic script, mundane-ish hypnosis.<br /> Obsession - A talk about how great something is.<br /> Paranoid - &quot;Everyone is out to get you, you are the victim here.&quot;<br /> Rampant - &quot;Magic is bitchin, why do anything else?&quot;<br /> Rapture - Read from the holy book.<br /> Shaken - Spooky story.<br /> Spooked - Story of the supernatural that isn't that scary.<br /> Steadfast - Uplifting and inspirational story that reaffirms their will.<br /> Swooning - Love poetry, etc.<br /> False Memories - Tell XYZ how it really happened! A &quot;news&quot; story.<br /> Wanton - Eat, drink and be merry, for tomorrow we die.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty broad power. That said, it costs 2 Glamour and requires an extended action that requires the target to sit down and listen to your speech, so other contracts are going to beat it out on efficiency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 06-05-2016, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}